    "done_when": "The independent review of the JT-60SA current signal maps measured two things the maps misstate, and this node corrects the text only; no rule, factor or source changes. (1) In imas_ambix/data/maps/jt-60sa/tf.json, the blocked cur2TFLKAT row no longer calls it a duplicate: on 60033 every sample is exactly 0.0 while cur1TFLKAT reads about 25.7 kA, and on 101154 both peak near 23.3 kA but correlate only 0.646 over the cached window. Its reason states those two measurements. (2) In imas_ambix/data/maps/jt-60sa/pf_active.json, the evidence of each served rule and each blocked chain says the chain choice rests on 101154 alone, because on 101173 and 60033 the coil currents sit at the noise floor (tens to a hundred A) and the chains do not corroborate it. Both measurements are re-derived by a test in tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py that reads /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/101154.zarr and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/60033.zarr read-only and asserts them (cur2TFLKAT all zero on 60033; cur1 and cur2 correlation on 101154 below 0.9), so the text cannot drift from the data. This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so the gate runs in place: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 4 tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py tests/data/test_signal_map.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?, exiting 0, with the gate log's first line naming the revision, the tree and the command. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. Nothing under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa is written and the JT-60SA server is never contacted.",
